---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../site';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy notice"
  description="What acqi.tech collects, why, how long it is kept, and who processes it."
>
  <section class="article-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="micro micro--red mb-1">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
      <div class="article-head__meta">
        <span class="micro">Last updated 17 November 2026</span>
        <span class="micro">Applies to acqi.tech</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose">
        <div class="note">
          <p>
            <strong>Status.</strong> ACQI Technologies is in formation and is not yet an
            incorporated data controller. Until incorporation, the founders are the controllers
            of the personal data described here. This notice will be reissued with the company's
            registration details on incorporation.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h2>What this notice covers</h2>
        <p>
          This notice covers the public website at acqi.tech, including the contact form and the
          password-gated product preview. It does not cover the product itself. When ACQI is
          installed in a customer environment, the customer is the controller of everything the
          product processes, and we are not a processor of that data.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Contact form.</strong> Name, email address, organisation, topic and message
            text. You choose what to write; please do not include confidential target data.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Server logs.</strong> The web host records the request path, timestamp,
            response code, user agent and IP address for every request. These are operational
            logs, kept for a short period for security and troubleshooting.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Preview session cookie.</strong> A single cookie named
            <code>acqi_preview</code>, set only after you enter the preview password. It holds a
            signed session token, expires after twelve hours, and is not used for anything except
            letting you move between preview screens.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do not use analytics, advertising, session recording, fingerprinting or any
          third-party script. There is no consent banner because there is nothing to consent to
          beyond the cookie described above, which is strictly necessary for a service you asked
          for.
        </p>

        <h2>Why we hold it</h2>
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Data</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Basis</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>Contact form content</td>
              <td>Replying to your enquiry and keeping a record of the conversation</td>
              <td>Legitimate interests in responding to a business enquiry; consent where you have given it</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Server logs</td>
              <td>Security, abuse prevention, fault diagnosis</td>
              <td>Legitimate interests in operating a safe service</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Preview cookie</td>
              <td>Maintaining a gate session you asked for</td>
              <td>Strictly necessary for the service</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>

        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Contact enquiries: while the conversation is live, then archived for up to two years.</li>
          <li>Server logs: up to thirty days, except where an entry is retained as evidence of abuse.</li>
          <li>Preview cookie: twelve hours from issue, or until you close the session.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Who processes it</h2>
        <p>
          The site is hosted on Microsoft Azure Static Web Apps in West US 2. Microsoft processes
          request logs and contact submissions on our instructions. No other processor receives
          data from this site. There is no marketing platform, no CRM and no email sequence.
        </p>
        <p>
          Because the host region is in the United States, a transfer outside the UK takes place.
          It is covered by the UK International Data Transfer Addendum to Microsoft's standard
          contractual clauses.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask for a copy of what we hold about you, ask for it to be corrected, ask for
          it to be deleted, or object to how it is used. Write to
          <a href={`mailto:${SITE.privacyEmail}`}>{SITE.privacyEmail}</a> and we will respond
          within one month. If you are unhappy with the response you can complain to the
          Information Commissioner's Office at ico.org.uk.
        </p>

        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>
          The site is served over TLS. The contact endpoint validates and length-limits input,
          discards obvious bot submissions, and does not echo submitted content back into a page.
          The preview gate uses a signed, time-limited cookie rather than a stored password in
          the browser. More detail is on the <a href="/security/">security page</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          This is a business website. It is not directed at children and we do not knowingly hold
          data about anyone under sixteen.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          Material changes will be marked with a new date at the top of this page. We do not
          maintain a mailing list, so we cannot notify you directly; the page is the notice.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Privacy questions: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.privacyEmail}`}>{SITE.privacyEmail}</a>.
          Security reports: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.securityEmail}`}>{SITE.securityEmail}</a>.
          Everything else: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.generalEmail}`}>{SITE.generalEmail}</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
